{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1272 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a7fc27bbdcf4cf0eef4981d23645f014e26b7da9622c1d1461a84b72061eff8f" :edb/db-before-t 1271 :edb/db-after-t 1272 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534584 50 #inst "2026-10-12T03:50:10.511Z" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186124484 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426551 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186124589 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426550 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186125219 1071 "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$\n- For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$\n- For any $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U,$ we have $[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x)=p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)].$" 13194139534584 17592186045417 false] [17592186125219 1071 "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$\n\nII. For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$\n\nIII. For any $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U,$ we have $[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x)=p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)].$" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186281525 1071 "Let $Q$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is a function $f(x)\\in Q,$ such that $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n- For any $f(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n- For any $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$" 13194139534584 17592186045417 false] [17592186281525 1071 "Let $Q$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. There is a function $f(x)\\in Q,$ such that $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n\nII. For any $f(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n\nIII. For any $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186360475 1071 "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- For any $A\\in R,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$\n- For any $A\\in R,$ we have $-1(-1\\cdot A)=-A.$\n- For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$" 13194139534584 17592186045417 false] [17592186360475 1071 "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. For any $A\\in R,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$\n\nII. For any $A\\in R,$ we have $-1(-1\\cdot A)=-A.$\n\nIII. For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426552 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426553 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426554 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426555 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1043 #edb/ref 17592186426556 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1045 "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1046 #edb/ref 17592186426552 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049737 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426537 1053 #uuid "ad1fad64-3179-5550-8fbd-b2cacb8f6bb0" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426538 1080 "II and III only" 13194