1080 "III only" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426546 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426546 1083 #uuid "96e40a22-66a9-56e3-b03b-cd6284f3fb8e" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426547 1080 "II only" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426547 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426547 1083 #uuid "d049396a-d59f-556c-a286-aabf743c306b" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426540 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426541 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426542 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426543 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426544 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1077 "selection" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426542 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426548 1079 #uuid "cd34e2b9-846d-52d4-a7f0-ad33a82569a5" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426538 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426539 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426545 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426546 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426547 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1077 "selection" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426539 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426549 1079 #uuid "ff55dda2-87d0-5c54-864b-9856103ddee8" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426550 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426548 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426550 1069 "q-162666" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426550 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426550 1071 "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $[\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ where $a\\in Z.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. For any $A\\in R,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A\\in R.$\n\nII. For any $A\\in R,$ we have $2\\cdot A\\in R.$\n\nIII. For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +1)A=\\alpha A+A.$" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426550 1072 #uuid "42098bc3-a0a9-510c-94ee-f777802bb49a" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426550 1074 "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example,the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\in R,$ since $4={2}^{2}$ and $2\\in Z.$ However\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\notin R,\n$$\n\nbecause a negative number ($-4$) can't be a square.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ from $R.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n2\\cdot A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\notin R\n$$\n\nbecause the $22$-entry of $2\\cdot A$ is not equal to $1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +1){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+{a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +1)A=\\alpha A+A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426551 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426549 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426551 1069 "q-162394" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426551 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426551 1071 "Let $E$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ that satisfy $f(0)=1.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The exponential function $f(x)={e}^{x}\\in E$\n\nII. For any $f(x),g(x)\\in E$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in E.$\n\nIII. The set $E$ is closed under addition." 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426551 1072 #uuid "ca37d526-e95e-5c72-ad4b-d05af7166afb" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426551 1074 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that\n\n$$\nf(0)={e}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\in E.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the function $f(x)=g(x)={e}^{x}\\in E.$ Then, \n\n$$\n(f+g)(0)={e}^{0}+{e}^{0}=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)+g(x)\\notin E.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $E$ is not closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426552 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426556 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426552 1062 #uuid "1f027f6f-3170-550b-8b2d-eb37f8a80677" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426552 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125219 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426553 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426555 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426553 1062 #uuid "3b196302-0187-5bfa-8880-a9d96466fbba" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426553 1063 #edb/ref 17592186426551 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426554 1062 #uuid "652a43ef-f276-5ff0-8235-02448f8f97ad" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426554 1063 #edb/ref 17592186426550 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426555 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426554 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426555 1062 #uuid "a1742ae5-ae23-562a-91d7-bbd1cf427a86" 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426555 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281525 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426556 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426553 13194139534584 17592186045417 true] [17592186426556 1062 #uuid "ea8e9bb5-f8d7-